      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Scientists justify mandates rather than just recommendations by pointing to the \"repercolation effect,\" where even a 1-2% disruption in vaccination coverage in unaffected areas can lead to prevented outbreaks in unaffected populations. This dynamic is driven by the \"herd effect,\" where intervening in one part of a community slows the overall spread of the virus across the entire network. Additionally, they argue that as a nation, we are one big public health \"pandemic\" and that such coordinated containment is necessary to benefit from the \"freeride\" of strong implementation in one area.",
